               <history>
                  <origin>
                     <origDate>s. xi ex--xii med</origDate>
                  </origin>
                  <provenance><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_36">Battle, Sussex. Benedictine abbey
                        of St Martin. </orgName><p>Hereford P.v.1 and Bodl. MS e Mus. 93, formed one
                        volume later at the cell of BRECON, q.v. See N. R. Ker, 'Sir John Prise',
                        The Library, 5th ser. 10 (1955), 7.</p><p>The Battle letter-mark is in this
                        book. Leland saw reference to the Historia Brittonum at Battle ('tantum in
                        indice'). Sir John Prise found a copy at Brecon, a cell of Battle, and noted
                        that it had been brought there from Battle by one of the monks, a detail
                        that fits with Leland's comment. D. Huws in National Library of Wales
                        Journal 17 (1971--2) 314--20, also argued that this is the historical volume
                        once owned by Prise and now divided across this MS and Bodl. ME e Musaeo 93
                        (s. xiimed).</p><q type="pressmark">EV</q></provenance>
               </history>
